.TH FATHOM_DRIFT 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-drift \- What the plan said against what the session did — the contradictions, both sides linked (`e4.8`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom drift\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-overlap\fR] [\fB\-\-max\fR] [\fB\-\-dismiss\fR] [\fB\-\-off\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-findings\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
What the plan said against what the session did — the contradictions, both sides linked (`e4.8`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fI<S>\fR
Compare one harness session only — its id, or `lineage:refs/heads/main` for the episodes no session was named for
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Read every episode in the index instead of the newest ones. A long read, and a longer report
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<N>\fR
How many episodes past a plan item to look for the change that did it
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-overlap\fR \fI<F>\fR
The token overlap at which a plan item counts as addressed (0.05 to 1.0)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\fR \fI<N>\fR
The cap on the report
.TP
\fB\-\-dismiss\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
A suppression key already argued about; its contradiction is counted, not re\-reported. Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-off\fR \fI<KIND>\fR
Switch one kind off, in the published spelling (`plan\-unimplemented`, …). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the report as JSON on stdout, and nothing else there
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-findings\fR
Exit 7 when anything was found, so a CI step can gate on it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
